<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>reproscope — {{ title }}</title>
<link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 100 100'><text y='.9em' font-size='90'>🔬</text></svg>">
<style>
:root{
  --ink:#16191d; --muted:#5d6672; --line:#d8dde5; --panel:#ffffff; --bg:#f6f7f9;
  --accent:#20456e; --warn:#8a5a00; --bad:#b3261e; --good:#1f6f43;
  --a:#c9e8d2; --b:#f6e6a8; --c:#f7cfa2; --f:#f3bdb8; --nf:#e6e8ec;
}
*{box-sizing:border-box}
body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);
  font:15px/1.55 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif}
.wrap{max-width:1120px;margin:0 auto;padding:28px 22px 80px}
h1{font-size:25px;line-height:1.25;margin:0 0 6px}
h2{font-size:19px;margin:34px 0 10px;padding-bottom:6px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--accent)}
h3{font-size:15px;margin:22px 0 8px;color:var(--accent)}
h4{font-size:14px;margin:16px 0 6px}
p{margin:8px 0}
a{color:var(--accent)}
code,pre{font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;font-size:12.5px}
pre{background:#f0f2f5;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;padding:10px;overflow-x:auto}
.panel{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0}
.muted{color:var(--muted)}
.small{font-size:13px}
.kv{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px 26px;margin:6px 0}
.kv div{font-size:13px}
.kv b{font-weight:600}
.scroll{overflow-x:auto;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch}
table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13px}
th,td{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:5px 8px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}
th{background:#eef1f5;font-weight:600}
td.n,th.n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.notrun{background:#eef0f3;border:1px dashed #b6bdc7;border-radius:8px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;color:var(--muted)}
.abstained{background:#fdf6e6;border:1px solid #e3cf95;border-radius:8px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0}
.howto{background:#eef4fb;border:1px solid #bcd0e8;border-left:5px solid var(--accent);
  border-radius:8px;padding:14px 18px;margin:16px 0}
.howto ul{margin:8px 0 0;padding-left:20px}
.conjecture{background:#fbf3f2;border:1px solid #e4bdb8;border-radius:8px;padding:6px 12px;
  display:inline-block;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--bad);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:6px}
.cell{text-align:center;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;white-space:nowrap}
.band-A{background:var(--a)} .band-B{background:var(--b)} .band-C{background:var(--c)}
.fail{background:var(--f)} .notfound{background:var(--nf);color:var(--muted)}
.cell.abstained{background:#fdf6e6;color:var(--warn)}
.failed{background:repeating-linear-gradient(45deg,#e6e8ec,#e6e8ec 5px,#cdd2da 5px,#cdd2da 10px);
  color:var(--muted)}
.headline td:first-child{border-left:4px solid var(--accent)}
.legend{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px 14px;font-size:12.5px;margin:8px 0}
.legend span{padding:2px 8px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:4px}
.pill{display:inline-block;padding:1px 7px;border-radius:10px;font-size:12px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:#eef1f5}
.pill.good{background:var(--a)} .pill.bad{background:var(--f)} .pill.warn{background:var(--b)}
details{margin:8px 0;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px;background:var(--panel)}
details>summary{cursor:pointer;padding:8px 12px;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600}
details[open]>summary{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
details .body{padding:10px 14px}
.md h1,.md h2{border:0;font-size:17px;margin:18px 0 6px;padding:0;color:var(--ink)}
.md h3{font-size:14.5px}
.md table{margin:8px 0}
.md blockquote{margin:8px 0;padding:2px 12px;border-left:3px solid var(--line);color:var(--muted)}
.grid2{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(320px,1fr));gap:14px}
.stat{display:inline-block;margin:0 22px 8px 0}
.stat b{display:block;font-size:20px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.stat span{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}
svg{max-width:100%;height:auto}
.foot{margin-top:40px;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:12px}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

{# ---------------- 1. header ---------------- #}
<h1>{{ title }}</h1>
<div class="kv">
  <div><b>paper_id</b> <code>{{ paper_id }}</code></div>
  {% if doi_url %}<div><b>DOI</b> <a href="{{ doi_url }}">{{ doi }}</a></div>{% endif %}
  <div><b>report built</b> {{ run_date }}</div>
  <div><b>API cost</b> ${{ '%.4f'|format(cost_api) }}</div>
  <div><b>subscription equivalent</b> ${{ '%.4f'|format(cost_equiv) }}</div>
  <div><b>model calls</b> {{ ledger.summary.total.calls }}</div>
</div>
<div class="kv">
  <div><b>models used</b>
  {% if ledger.models %}{{ ledger.models|join(', ') }}{% else %}<span class="muted">no ledger rows</span>{% endif %}
  </div>
</div>

{# ---------------- 2. how to read ---------------- #}
<div class="howto">
  <h3 style="margin-top:0">How to read this report</h3>
  <p><b>The stages carry different weight.</b> Stage 1 findings are worth acting on: they point at
  methods that need to be specified more clearly, or at numbers that need fixing. Stages 2 and 3
  are context for a human reviewer, not verdicts on the paper.</p>
  <p><b>Every claim ends in one of two states</b> — <i>complete</i> or <i>abstained</i>. An
  abstention is a recorded refusal with a reason (the estimand could not be bound to the data, an
  input was missing). Abstentions are excluded from the summary rates, so a replica that says
  "cannot be attempted" is never scored below one that guesses.</p>
  <p><b>What a match means.</b> A close match shows that one route to the reported number exists.
  A mismatch does not identify whether the paper or the replicas are wrong (or underspecified).
  It triggers the targeted reconstruction and the diagnosis pass, and should be read jointly with
  the dispersion metric, the re-run arm where present, and Stage 3.</p>
  <p class="small muted">Replicas work from a redacted methods document and never see the reported
  values. Bands are tolerance classes, not pass/fail: A within 2%, B within 20%, C within 40%,
  with quantity-specific rules for p values, ratios and counts. Raw and standardised differences
  are shown next to every band.</p>
</div>

{# ---------------- 3. focal claim ---------------- #}
<h2>Focal claim</h2>
<div class="panel">
  {% if focal.text %}<p style="font-size:16px">“{{ focal.text }}”</p>{% endif %}
  <div class="kv">
    {% if focal.source %}<div><b>source</b> {{ focal.source }}</div>{% endif %}
    <div><b>claim id</b> {% if focal.claim_id %}<code>{{ focal.claim_id }}</code>{% else %}<span class="muted">unresolved</span>{% endif %}</div>
    {% if focal.quantity_kind %}<div><b>quantity</b> {{ focal.quantity_kind }}</div>{% endif %}
  </div>
  <p class="small muted">Identified by: {{ focal.rule }}.</p>

  <div class="grid2">
    <div>
      <h4>Reported in the paper</h4>
      {% if focal.reported %}
      <table>
        {% for k, v in focal.reported.items() %}
        {% if v is not none %}<tr><th>{{ k }}</th><td>{{ v|num if v is number else v }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      </table>
      {% else %}<p class="muted">no reported statistic in the manifest</p>{% endif %}
    </div>
    <div>
      <h4>Multi100 analysts (Cohen's d)</h4>
      {% if focal.multi100 and focal.multi100.analyst_d %}
      <table>
        <tr><th>analysts</th><td class="n">{{ focal.multi100.n_analysts }}</td></tr>
        {% for k in ['min','median','max'] %}
        <tr><th>d {{ k }}</th><td class="n">{{ focal.multi100.analyst_d.get(k)|num }}</td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </table>
      <p class="small muted">These are standardised mean differences. Compare them with a
      reproscope value only where that value is also a <i>d</i>.</p>
      {% else %}
      <p class="muted">No Multi100 record in the manifest for this paper.</p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    <div>
      <h4>reproscope replicas, this claim</h4>
      {% if focal.claim and focal.claim.value is not none %}
      <p class="small">Claim <code>{{ focal.claim_id }}</code> as reported:
      <b>{{ focal.claim.value }}</b>{% if focal.quantity_kind %} ({{ focal.quantity_kind }}){% endif %}</p>
      {% endif %}
      {% if focal.replica_values %}
      <table>
        <tr><th>replica</th><th class="n">value</th><th>band</th></tr>
        {% for r in focal.replica_values %}
        <tr><td><code>{{ r.replica_id }}</code></td><td class="n">{{ r.value }}</td>
            <td>{% if r.band %}<span class="pill {{ 'good' if r.band in ['A','B'] else 'bad' }}">{{ r.band }}</span>{% else %}—{% endif %}</td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </table>
      {% else %}
      <p class="muted">No Stage 1 comparison rows for this claim.</p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{# ---------------- 4. stage 0 ---------------- #}
<h2>Stage 0 — Intake, extraction and data readiness</h2>
{% if not s0 %}
<div class="notrun"><b>Stage 0 not run.</b> No artifacts under <code>stage0/</code>, so there are no
claim records, estimand contracts, readiness record or redaction report for this paper.</div>
{% else %}
<div class="panel">
  <div>
    <span class="stat"><b>{{ s0.n_claims }}</b><span>claims extracted</span></span>
    {% for k, v in s0.by_importance %}<span class="stat"><b>{{ v }}</b><span>{{ k }}</span></span>{% endfor %}
    {% for k, v in s0.by_type %}<span class="stat"><b>{{ v }}</b><span>type: {{ k }}</span></span>{% endfor %}
    <span class="stat">
      <b>{% if s0.extraction.rate is not none %}{{ s0.extraction.rate|pct }}{% else %}n/a{% endif %}</b>
      <span>two-model extraction agreement</span></span>
  </div>
  {% if s0.extraction.n_with_records == 0 %}
  <p class="small muted">No <code>extraction</code> records on the claims, so the two-model
  agreement rate could not be computed (this is not a 0% agreement).</p>
  {% else %}
  <p class="small muted">{{ s0.extraction.n_agreed }} of {{ s0.extraction.n_with_records }} claims
  agreed between the two extraction models before arbitration.</p>
  {% endif %}
</div>

<h3>Estimand contracts</h3>
{% if s0.contracts %}
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <tr><th>analysis</th><th>model type</th><th>sample rule</th><th>outcome</th><th>claims</th>
      <th class="n">ambiguities</th><th>state</th><th>readiness</th></tr>
  {% for c in s0.contracts %}
  <tr>
    <td><code>{{ c.analysis_id }}</code></td>
    <td>{{ c.model_type or '—' }}</td>
    <td>{{ c.sample_rule or '—' }}</td>
    <td>{{ c.outcome or '—' }}</td>
    <td>{{ c.claim_ids|join(', ') }}</td>
    <td class="n">{{ c.ambiguities|length }}</td>
    <td><span class="pill {{ 'bad' if c.state == 'abstained' else '' }}">{{ c.state or '—' }}</span></td>
    <td><span class="pill {{ 'bad' if c.readiness_state == 'abstained' else '' }}">{{ c.readiness_state or '—' }}</span></td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table></div>
{% for c in s0.contracts %}{% if c.ambiguities %}
<details><summary>Ambiguities recorded for <code>{{ c.analysis_id }}</code> ({{ c.ambiguities|length }})</summary>
<div class="body"><table>
  <tr><th>field</th><th>options</th><th>note</th></tr>
  {% for a in c.ambiguities %}
  <tr><td>{{ a.field }}</td><td>{{ (a.options or [])|join(' · ') }}</td><td>{{ a.note or '' }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table></div></details>
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
{% else %}
<p class="muted">No contracts recorded.</p>
{% endif %}

<h3>Data readiness</h3>
{% if s0.readiness %}
<div class="panel">
  <div class="kv">
    <div><b>unit of observation</b> {{ s0.readiness.unit_of_observation or '—' }}</div>
    <div><b>keys</b> {{ (s0.readiness['keys'] or [])|join(', ') or '—' }}</div>
    <div><b>missing sentinels</b> {{ (s0.readiness.missing_sentinels or [])|join(', ') or 'none' }}</div>
    <div><b>state</b> {{ s0.readiness.state or '—' }}</div>
  </div>
  {% if s0.readiness.files %}
  <table>
    <tr><th>file</th><th>format</th><th class="n">rows</th><th class="n">cols</th></tr>
    {% for f in s0.readiness.files %}
    <tr><td><code>{{ f.path }}</code></td><td>{{ f.format or '—' }}</td>
        <td class="n">{{ f.rows if f.rows is not none else '—' }}</td>
        <td class="n">{{ f.cols if f.cols is not none else '—' }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% endif %}
  <h4>Variable bindings</h4>
  {% if s0.bindings %}
  <table>
    <tr><th>contract field</th><th>candidate columns</th><th>chosen</th><th>note</th></tr>
    {% for b in s0.bindings %}
    <tr{% if b.unbound %} class="fail"{% endif %}>
      <td>{{ b.field }}</td><td>{{ b.candidates|join(', ') }}</td>
      <td>{% if b.chosen %}<code>{{ b.chosen }}</code>{% else %}<b>unbound (null)</b>{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{{ b.note or '' }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% else %}
  <p class="muted">No variable bindings recorded. Nothing was left for a human to resolve, or the
  readiness step did not enumerate bindings.</p>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% else %}
<div class="notrun">No readiness record.</div>
{% endif %}

<h3>Blinding: redaction and leakage audit</h3>
{% if s0.redaction %}
<div class="panel">
  <div class="kv">
    <div><b>deterministic value scan</b>
      <span class="pill {{ 'good' if s0.redaction.scan_clean else 'bad' }}">
        {{ 'clean' if s0.redaction.scan_clean else 'HITS' }}</span></div>
    <div><b>scan hits</b> {{ (s0.redaction.scan_hits or [])|length }}</div>
    <div><b>spans removed</b> {{ (s0.redaction.removed_spans or [])|length }}</div>
    <div><b>leakage audit</b>
      <span class="pill {{ 'good' if s0.leak_verdict == 'clean' else 'warn' }}">{{ s0.leak_verdict or 'not run' }}</span></div>
  </div>
  {% if s0.leak_note %}<p class="small">{{ s0.leak_note }}</p>{% endif %}
  {% if s0.redaction.scan_hits %}
  <p class="small"><b>Hits (blocking):</b> {{ s0.redaction.scan_hits|join(', ') }}</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% if s0.redaction.removed_spans %}
  <table>
    <tr><th>kind</th><th>location</th><th>text</th></tr>
    {% for r in s0.redaction.removed_spans %}
    <tr><td>{{ r.kind }}</td><td>{{ r.location or '—' }}</td><td>{{ r.text or '—' }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% else %}
<div class="notrun">No redaction report. The blinding step did not run or wrote no sidecar.</div>
{% endif %}

{% if s0.has_methods %}
<details><summary>Redacted methods document given to the replicas</summary>
<div class="body md">{{ s0.methods_html }}</div></details>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{# ---------------- 5. stage 1 ---------------- #}
<h2>Stage 1 — Computational reproduction</h2>
{% if not s1 %}
<div class="notrun"><b>Stage 1 not run.</b> No <code>stage1/</code> artifacts: no blind replicas, no
match table, no targeted reconstruction and no diagnosis for this paper.</div>
{% else %}

<h3>Match table</h3>
<p class="small muted">Rows are claims, headline first; columns are blind replicas. Each cell shows
the value the replica computed, coloured by tolerance band. Hover a cell for the raw and
standardised differences.</p>
<div class="legend">
  <span class="band-A">A — within 2%</span><span class="band-B">B — within 20%</span>
  <span class="band-C">C — within 40%</span><span class="fail">fail / sign mismatch</span>
  <span class="notfound">claim not found by this replica</span>
  <span class="cell abstained">abstained — no evidence either way</span>
  <span class="failed">replica failed to run</span>
</div>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <tr>
    <th>claim</th><th>quantity</th><th class="n">reported</th>
    {% for rid in s1.replica_ids %}<th class="n">{{ rid }}</th>{% endfor %}
    <th class="n">fraction matched</th><th class="n">numeric CV</th><th class="n">decision agreement</th>
  </tr>
  {% for r in s1.table %}
  <tr{% if r.importance == 'headline' %} class="headline"{% endif %}>
    <td><code>{{ r.claim_id }}</code>
      {% if r.importance %}<br><span class="small muted">{{ r.importance }}</span>{% endif %}
      {% if r.description %}<br><span class="small">{{ r.description }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
    <td>{{ r.quantity_kind or '—' }}</td>
    <td class="n">{{ r.reported }}</td>
    {% for c in r.cells %}
    <td class="cell {{ c.state }}" title="{{ c.detail }}">{{ c.label }}{% if c.band %}<br><span class="small">{{ c.band }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
    {% endfor %}
    <td class="n">{{ r.fraction_matched|pct }}</td>
    <td class="n">{{ r.numeric_cv|num }}</td>
    <td class="n">{{ r.decision_agreement|num }}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table></div>

<h3>Replicas</h3>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <tr><th>replica</th><th>family</th><th>model</th><th>route</th><th>tier</th><th>ran</th>
      <th class="n">fixes (min/maj/crit)</th><th>hardcoding audit</th><th class="n">turns</th>
      <th class="n">tokens in/out</th><th class="n">cost $</th></tr>
  {% for r in s1.replicas %}
  <tr>
    <td><code>{{ r.replica_id }}</code></td>
    <td>{{ r.family or '—' }}</td><td>{{ r.model or '—' }}</td><td>{{ r.route or '—' }}</td>
    <td>{{ r.tier }}</td>
    <td>{% if r.ran %}<span class="pill good">yes</span>{% else %}<span class="pill bad">no</span>{% endif %}</td>
    <td class="n">{{ r.fix_counts.minor }}/{{ r.fix_counts.major }}/{{ r.fix_counts.critical }}{% if r.fix_counts.unrated %} (+{{ r.fix_counts.unrated }} unrated){% endif %}</td>
    <td>{% if r.hardcoding %}<span class="pill {{ 'good' if r.hardcoding == 'clean' else 'bad' }}">{{ r.hardcoding }}</span>{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
    <td class="n">{{ r.turns if r.turns is not none else '—' }}</td>
    <td class="n">{% if r.usage %}{{ r.usage.tokens_in|int }} / {{ r.usage.tokens_out|int }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
    <td class="n">{% if r.usage %}{{ '%.4f'|format(r.usage.cost_usd) }}{% if r.usage.cost_usd_equiv %} <span class="muted">({{ '%.4f'|format(r.usage.cost_usd_equiv) }} equiv)</span>{% endif %}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table></div>
<p class="small muted">Turns are the agent's repair loops recorded in <code>run_checks</code>.
Token and cost figures are joined from the ledger on <code>replica_id</code>; a subscription route
bills $0 and reports a list-price equivalent instead.</p>

<h3>Cheap versus frontier replicas</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>tier</th><th>replicas</th><th class="n">cells in band A or B</th><th class="n">comparable cells</th><th class="n">match rate</th></tr>
  {% for s in s1.split %}
  <tr><td>{{ s.tier }}{% if s.tier == 'frontier' %} <span class="small muted">(claude_p, codex)</span>{% else %} <span class="small muted">(openrouter, opencode)</span>{% endif %}</td>
      <td>{{ s.replicas|join(', ') or '—' }}</td>
      <td class="n">{{ s.matched }}</td><td class="n">{{ s.comparable }}</td><td class="n">{{ s.rate|pct }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
<p class="small muted">The split is by model route, which is the only tier signal recorded in the
traces. Comparable cells exclude claims a replica did not find and replicas that did not run.</p>

<h3>Targeted reconstruction</h3>
{% if not s1.targeted %}
<div class="notrun">No <code>targeted.json</code>: the targeted reconstruction arm did not run.</div>
{% else %}
<div class="panel">
  <div class="kv">
    <div><b>triggered</b> {{ 'yes' if s1.targeted.triggered else 'no' }}</div>
    <div><b>outcome</b> <span class="pill {{ 'bad' if s1.targeted.outcome in ['not_reachable','reachable_indefensibly'] else ('warn' if s1.targeted.outcome == 'abstained' else '') }}">{{ s1.targeted.outcome }}</span></div>
    <div><b>attempts</b> {{ s1.targeted.attempts }}</div>
  </div>
  {% if s1.targeted.notes %}<p>{{ s1.targeted.notes }}</p>{% endif %}
  <h4>Choices the reconstruction had to add</h4>
  {% if s1.targeted.added_choices %}
  <ul>{% for c in s1.targeted.added_choices %}<li>{{ c }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
  {% else %}<p class="muted">None. (When the arm is triggered and reaches the reported number, this
  list is what the paper should have stated.)</p>{% endif %}
</div>
{% endif %}

<h3>Re-run of the original code</h3>
{% if not s1.rerun %}
<div class="notrun">No <code>rerun.json</code>: the re-run arm did not run.</div>
{% elif s1.rerun.state == 'abstained' %}
<div class="abstained"><b>Abstained.</b> {{ s1.rerun.abstain_reason or 'no reason recorded' }}
<p class="small">The reproduction therefore shows that the supplied data yields the reported
numbers, not that the reported numbers came from that data.</p></div>
{% else %}
<div class="panel"><pre>{{ s1.rerun|tojson(indent=2) }}</pre></div>
{% endif %}

{% if s1.trace_equivalence %}
<details><summary>Decision-trace equivalence across replicas (agreement {{ s1.trace_equivalence.agreement|num }})</summary>
<div class="body">
  <table><tr><th>field</th><th>groups</th><th>note</th></tr>
  {% for f in s1.trace_equivalence.fields or [] %}
  <tr><td>{{ f.field }}</td>
      <td>{% for g in f.groups %}<code>{{ g|join(', ') }}</code>{% if not loop.last %} vs {% endif %}{% endfor %}</td>
      <td>{{ f.note }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}</table>
  {% if s1.trace_equivalence.notable_divergences %}
  <h4>Notable divergences</h4>
  <ul>{% for d in s1.trace_equivalence.notable_divergences %}<li>{{ d }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
  {% endif %}
</div></details>
{% endif %}

<h3>Divergence diagnosis</h3>
{% if not s1.has_diagnosis %}
<div class="notrun">No <code>diagnosis.md</code>: the diagnosis pass did not run.</div>
{% else %}
<div class="conjecture">Conjecture — unblinded, not evidence</div>
<div class="panel md">{{ s1.diagnosis_html }}</div>
{% endif %}

<h3>Open choices per replica</h3>
{% for r in s1.replicas %}
<details><summary><code>{{ r.replica_id }}</code> — {{ r.open_choices|length }} open choice(s){% if r.details %}, {{ r.details|length }} trace field(s){% endif %}</summary>
<div class="body">
  {% if r.open_choices %}
  <ul>{% for c in r.open_choices %}
  <li>{% if c is mapping %}
    <b>{{ c.get('open') or c.get('choice') or 'choice' }}</b>
    {% if c.get('options') %}<br><span class="small muted">options: {{ c.get('options')|join(' · ') }}</span>{% endif %}
    {% if c.get('chosen') %}<br>chose: <b>{{ c.get('chosen') }}</b>{% endif %}
    {% if c.get('why') %}<br><span class="small">{{ c.get('why') }}</span>{% endif %}
  {% else %}{{ c }}{% endif %}</li>
  {% endfor %}</ul>
  {% else %}<p class="muted">No open choices recorded.</p>{% endif %}
  {% if r.fixes %}
  <h4>Fixes</h4>
  <ul>{% for f in r.fixes %}<li>[{{ f.severity or 'unrated' }}] {{ f.description }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
  {% endif %}
  {% if r.hardcoding_hits %}
  <h4>Hardcoding audit hits</h4><pre>{{ r.hardcoding_hits|tojson(indent=2) }}</pre>
  {% endif %}
  {% for k, v in r.details %}
  <h4>{{ k }}</h4><pre>{{ v }}</pre>
  {% endfor %}
</div></details>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{# ---------------- 6. stage 2 ---------------- #}
<h2>Stage 2 — Analysis review <span class="small muted">(context, not a verdict)</span></h2>
{% if not s2 %}
<div class="notrun"><b>Stage 2 not run.</b> No <code>stage2/</code> artifacts: no causal-language
rating, no minimum-detectable-effect curve, no alignment check and no referee-style pass.</div>
{% else %}
<div class="panel">
  <div class="kv">
    {% if s2.claim_id %}<div><b>focal claim</b> <code>{{ s2.claim_id }}</code></div>{% endif %}
    {% if s2.causal %}<div><b>causal language</b> <span class="pill warn">{{ s2.causal.verdict or s2.causal.rating }}</span></div>{% endif %}
    {% if s2.mde %}<div><b>MDE at 80% power</b> {{ s2.mde.mde_standardised|num }} {{ s2.mde.mde_metric or '' }}</div>{% endif %}
    {% if s2.alignment %}<div><b>claim–analysis alignment</b> <span class="pill">{{ s2.alignment.verdict }}</span></div>{% endif %}
    <div><b>broad findings</b> {{ s2.findings|length }}</div>
  </div>
</div>
{% if s2.has_md %}
<div class="panel md">{{ s2.review_html }}</div>
{% else %}
<div class="notrun">No <code>review.md</code>; only the structured record exists.</div>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{# ---------------- 7. stage 3 ---------------- #}
<h2>Stage 3 — Multiverse robustness <span class="small muted">(context, not a verdict)</span></h2>
{% if not s3 %}
<div class="notrun"><b>Stage 3 not run.</b> No <code>stage3/</code> artifacts: no specification
space, no multiverse runs and no specification curve.</div>
{% else %}
<div class="panel">
  <div>
    <span class="stat"><b>{{ s3.grid_size if s3.grid_size is not none else '—' }}</b><span>full grid size</span></span>
    <span class="stat"><b>{{ s3.n_specs }}</b><span>specifications executed</span></span>
    <span class="stat"><b>{{ s3.n_converged }}</b><span>converged</span></span>
    <span class="stat"><b>{{ s3.reported_estimate|num }}</b><span>reported estimate</span></span>
    <span class="stat"><b>{{ s3.median|num }}</b><span>multiverse median</span></span>
    <span class="stat"><b>{{ s3.share_same_sign|pct }}</b><span>same sign</span></span>
    <span class="stat"><b>{{ s3.share_p05|pct }}</b><span>p &lt; .05</span></span>
    <span class="stat"><b>{{ s3.extremeness|num }}</b><span>extremeness</span></span>
  </div>
  <p><b>Rank of the reported estimate:</b>
  {% if s3.rank is not none %}
    {{ s3.rank }} of {{ s3.n_specs }}{% if s3.rank > s3.n_specs %} — the paper's value sits above
    every specification in the multiverse{% endif %}.
  {% else %}not computed.{% endif %}
  {% if s3.range[0] is not none %}
  Multiverse estimates run from {{ s3.range[0]|num }} to {{ s3.range[1]|num }}.{% endif %}
  {% if s3.sampled %}
  <br><b>Sampled.</b> The {{ s3.n_specs }} specifications executed are a
  {{ s3.sample_fraction|pct }} stratified sample of the full grid of
  {{ s3.grid_size }}; the figures above describe that sample, not the whole multiverse.
  {% endif %}
  {% if s3.focal_quantity.kind %} The focal quantity is <b>{{ s3.focal_quantity.kind }}</b>
  (claim <code>{{ s3.claim_id }}</code>).{% endif %}</p>
</div>

<h3>Specification curve</h3>
{% if s3.svg %}
{{ s3.svg }}
<p class="small muted">Each point is one specification, sorted by estimate. The red line is the
estimate reported in the paper. A ringed point is the paper-level specification (every factor at
the level the paper used); no ring means the paper-level combination is not in the grid or the
factors do not all record a paper level.</p>
{% else %}
<div class="notrun">No numeric estimates to plot.</div>
{% endif %}

<h3>Factors and levels</h3>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <tr><th>factor</th><th>source</th><th>level</th><th>verdict</th><th>rationale / how</th></tr>
  {% for f in s3.factors %}
    {% for l in f.levels %}
    <tr>
      {% if loop.first %}<td rowspan="{{ f.levels|length }}"><b>{{ f.name }}</b>
        {% if f.field %}<br><span class="small muted">{{ f.field }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
      <td rowspan="{{ f.levels|length }}">{{ f.source or '—' }}</td>{% endif %}
      <td>{{ l.value }}{% if f.paper_level == l.value %} <span class="pill">paper level</span>{% endif %}</td>
      <td><span class="pill {{ 'good' if l.verdict == 'defensible' else 'bad' }}">{{ l.verdict or '—' }}</span></td>
      <td>{{ l.rationale or l.how or '—' }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  {% endfor %}
</table></div>
{% if s3.incompatibilities %}
<p class="small"><b>Incompatible combinations:</b>
{% for i in s3.incompatibilities %}<code>{{ i|join(' + ') }}</code>{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>
{% endif %}
{% if s3.dropped_factors %}
<p class="small"><b>Dropped factors:</b> {{ s3.dropped_factors|join(', ') }}</p>
{% endif %}

<details><summary>All {{ s3.runs|length }} specification runs</summary>
<div class="body scroll"><table>
  <tr>
    {% for k in (s3.runs[0].spec.keys() if s3.runs else []) %}<th>{{ k }}</th>{% endfor %}
    <th class="n">estimate</th><th class="n">se</th><th class="n">p</th><th>converged</th></tr>
  {% for r in s3.runs %}
  <tr>{% for v in r.spec.values() %}<td>{{ v }}</td>{% endfor %}
    <td class="n">{{ r.estimate|num }}</td><td class="n">{{ r.se|num }}</td>
    <td class="n">{{ r.p|num }}</td><td>{{ 'yes' if r.converged else 'no' }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table></div></details>

<h3>Interpretation</h3>
{% if s3.interpretation_html %}
<div class="panel md">{{ s3.interpretation_html }}</div>
{% else %}
<div class="notrun">No interpretation written.</div>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{# ---------------- 8. appendix ---------------- #}
<h2>Appendix</h2>

<h3>Model-call ledger</h3>
{% if ledger.table %}
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <tr><th>stage</th><th>model</th><th>route</th><th class="n">calls</th><th class="n">tokens in</th>
      <th class="n">tokens out</th><th class="n">API $</th><th class="n">subscription-equivalent $</th></tr>
  {% for r in ledger.table %}
  <tr><td>{{ r.stage }}</td><td>{{ r.model }}</td><td>{{ r.route }}</td>
      <td class="n">{{ r.calls }}</td><td class="n">{{ r.tokens_in|int }}</td>
      <td class="n">{{ r.tokens_out|int }}</td><td class="n">{{ '%.4f'|format(r.cost_usd) }}</td>
      <td class="n">{{ '%.4f'|format(r.cost_usd_equiv) }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  <tr><th>TOTAL</th><th></th><th></th><th class="n">{{ ledger.summary.total.calls }}</th>
      <th class="n">{{ ledger.summary.total.tokens_in|int }}</th>
      <th class="n">{{ ledger.summary.total.tokens_out|int }}</th>
      <th class="n">{{ '%.4f'|format(cost_api) }}</th>
      <th class="n">{{ '%.4f'|format(cost_equiv) }}</th></tr>
</table></div>
<p class="small muted">API $ excludes subscription routes (claude_p, codex), which bill nothing at
the margin; their list-price equivalent is shown separately and is never added to the API total.</p>
{% else %}
<div class="notrun">No ledger rows for this paper.</div>
{% endif %}

<h3>Environment</h3>
<div class="panel">
  <p class="small">Replicas ran locally on the pilot machine's R and Python installations. No
  container was used, so package versions are those present on the machine. Every replica trace
  records <code>sessionInfo()</code> or <code>pip freeze</code> so version-sensitive defaults stay
  visible. This is a recorded deviation from the pinned image in the scope document.</p>
  {% if manifest.environment %}
  <div class="kv"><div><b>language hint</b> {{ manifest.environment.get('language_hint') or '—' }}</div>
  <div><b>versions named in the paper</b> {{ manifest.environment.get('versions_named') or 'none' }}</div></div>
  {% endif %}
  {% if session_info %}
  <h4>sessionInfo excerpt (from a replica trace)</h4>
  <pre>{{ session_info }}</pre>
  {% else %}
  <p class="muted small">No trace recorded a sessionInfo block.</p>
  {% endif %}
</div>

<h3>Attached artifacts</h3>
{% if attachments %}
<p class="small muted">Paths are relative to <code>runs/{{ paper_id }}/</code>. The machine-readable
chain is in <code>report/report.json</code> next to this file.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <tr><th>path</th><th class="n">KB</th></tr>
  {% for a in attachments %}
  <tr><td><code>{{ a.path }}</code></td><td class="n">{{ a.size_kb if a.size_kb is not none else '' }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table></div>
{% else %}
<p class="muted">No artifacts on disk for this paper.</p>
{% endif %}

<div class="foot">
reproscope v0 pilot · report for <code>{{ paper_id }}</code> built {{ run_date }}.
Stage 1 findings are worth acting on; Stages 2 and 3 are context for a human reviewer.
</div>

</div>
</body>
</html>
